            <ArticleTitle>Association between metabolic syndrome and subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in asymptomatic adults.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1554-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Metabolic syndrome was associated with the presence and quantity of coronary artery calcium, a marker of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis, in 1,129 asymptomatic adults, ages 20 to 79 years, from a community-based study. The association was independent of 10-year risk of coronary heart disease based on the Framingham risk score.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
